{"step": 10, "raw_content": "Now I understand the project. There's no YAML library, so I need to parse the YAML manually. The structure is simple and I need to handle:\n\n1. File missing → dispatch normally (preserve behavior)\n2. Section `notifications` missing → dispatch normally\n3. Flag `email_dispatch_enabled` missing → dispatch normally\n4. Flag explicitly `false` → suppress dispatch\n5. Flag `true` → dispatch normally\n\nLet me implement a helper in `src/common/settings.py` to load the feature flag, following the existing `config_path` and `load_retry_policy` pattern.\n\nLet me write a simple YAML parser for this specific structure. The YAML format is:\n```yaml\nnotifications:\n  email_dispatch_enabled: false\n```\n\nI'll parse it robustly. Let me add a function to `settings.py`:", "native_tool_calls": [{"call_id": "step-10-call-1", "provider_call_id": "call_00_CA1Qrg1BStn1nyvEIN3Q4980", "name": "apply_patch", "arguments": {"edits": [{"path": "src/common/settings.py", "content": "\"\"\"Configuration loading helpers.\"\"\"\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\ndef config_path(name: str) -> Path:\n    return Path(\"configs\") / name\n\n\ndef load_retry_policy() -> dict:\n    return {\"initial_delay_seconds\": 30, \"max_attempts\": 5}\n\n\ndef load_feature_flag(section: str, flag: str) -> bool | None:\n    \"\"\"Read a boolean feature flag from configs/feature_flags.yaml.\n\n    Returns None when the file, section, or flag is missing so callers can\n    preserve their default behavior.\n    \"\"\"\n    path = config_path(\"feature_flags.yaml\")\n    if not path.exists():\n        return None\n\n    current_section: str | None = None\n    for raw_line in path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines():\n        line = raw_line.strip()\n        if not line or line.startswith(\"#\"):\n            continue\n        if line.endswith(\":\"):\n            current_section = line[:-1].strip()\n            continue\n        if \":\" not in line:\n            continue\n        key, _, value = line.partition(\":\")\n        key = key.strip()\n        value = value.strip()\n        if current_section == section and key == flag:\n            if value.lower() == \"false\":\n                return False\n            if value.lower() == \"true\":\n                return True\n            return None\n    return None\n"}]}}], "dialect": null, "canonical_payload": {"tool_calls": [{"name": "apply_patch", "arguments": {"edits": [{"path": "src/common/settings.py", "content": "\"\"\"Configuration loading helpers.\"\"\"\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\ndef config_path(name: str) -> Path:\n    return Path(\"configs\") / name\n\n\ndef load_retry_policy() -> dict:\n    return {\"initial_delay_seconds\": 30, \"max_attempts\": 5}\n\n\ndef load_feature_flag(section: str, flag: str) -> bool | None:\n    \"\"\"Read a boolean feature flag from configs/feature_flags.yaml.\n\n    Returns None when the file, section, or flag is missing so callers can\n    preserve their default behavior.\n    \"\"\"\n    path = config_path(\"feature_flags.yaml\")\n    if not path.exists():\n        return None\n\n    current_section: str | None = None\n    for raw_line in path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines():\n        line = raw_line.strip()\n        if not line or line.startswith(\"#\"):\n            continue\n        if line.endswith(\":\"):\n            current_section = line[:-1].strip()\n            continue\n        if \":\" not in line:\n            continue\n        key, _, value = line.partition(\":\")\n        key = key.strip()\n        value = value.strip()\n        if current_section == section and key == flag:\n            if value.lower() == \"false\":\n                return False\n            if value.lower() == \"true\":\n                return True\n            return None\n    return None\n"}]}, "runtime_call_id": "step-10-call-1", "provider_call_id": "call_00_CA1Qrg1BStn1nyvEIN3Q4980"}]}, "parse_error": null, "model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "provider": "openai-compatible", "response_id": "9441cea6-be0e-4c6d-84ad-c4305d5a84f3", "finish_state": "tool_calls", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "actual_response_mode": "native_tools", "incomplete_reason": null, "system_fingerprint": "a307abda487cd1b463329ccb945ce396", "input_tokens": 7575, "output_tokens": 606}
